        "topic": "Metal extraction methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2013",
        "question_text": "<p>The process of extracting iron from its ore using a blast furnace involves the reduction of <b>haematite</b> ($Fe_2O_3$) with which of the following?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) by reducing it with carbon monoxide ($CO$), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The chemical equation for the reduction is: $Fe_2O_3 + 3CO \rightarrow 2Fe + 3CO_2$.</p>",
